Bristlebind was used by [[Dante Vale]] to bind the legs of [[Ymir]] in search of the [[Temple of Thor]]. The giant [[Titans|Titan]] tumbled but was able to get up after a few seconds, giving the Huntik team some time to get away from it. {{source|The Legacy of Thor}}

Dante Vale used the spell in an attempt to slow down [[Grier]] when they were fighting one-on-one in [[Sutos Island]]. {{source|Like Father, Unlike Son}}

On the Huntik team's way to the [[Golden Asp]], [[Lok Lambert]] used Bristlebind in combination with [[Zhalia Moon]]'s [[Darkfog]] spell to flip an [[The Organization|Organization]] car who was following them multiple times. Darkfog made it so the driver couldn't see the incoming vines. {{source|The Golden Asp}}

[[Marduk]] also used this spell to ensnare Dante Vale's [[Metagolem]] in [[Mexico]] during the search for the [[Rings|Ring]] of [[Quetzalcoatl]]. Metagolem struggled for a short moment, but he was quickly able to break the vines and take out an [[Harlekin]] Titan attacking him. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

[[Lane]] used Bristlebind to restrain one of many [[Silent Soldiers]] in a massive war against the [[Blood Spirals]] by the [[Fortress of Iron Will]].{{source|The Spiral War}}

This spell was used by Dante Vale in conjunction with [[Stopglue]] to heavily detain [[Hoffman]] when the two were fighting in [[The Professor's castle|The Professor's Castle]]. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

[[Scarlet Byrne]] used Bristlebind to bind the legs of a [[Firbolg]] Titan the Huntik team encountered when exploring [[Tír na nÓg]]. This allowed [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[Kaioh the Tracker]] to freely strike the Titan, taking him out. {{source|Back Home}}

